CORE
contract.sol
--contract TupleRet --solidity-path-coverage --solidity-max-tx 1 --path-cov-assert spec.json
^WARNING: --path-cov-assert: 2 state variable\(s\) carry NO candidate and appear in NO row below: return \(the unit returns a value, but no scalar return ghost could be built for it
A tuple / struct / dynamic return emits no RETURN instruction carrying a single renderable operand
Its absence from this table is a REFUSAL, not a measurement that the value is unconstrained
^--path-cov-assert: region NON-VACUITY witnessed
^--path-cov-assert: total: post == pre  HOLDS$
^--path-cov-assert: total: post != pre  REFUTED
^--path-cov-assert: ladder summary -- 6 candidate\(s\): 3 HOLDS, 3 REFUTED, 0 no verdict \(solver unknown\), 0 no verdict \(never reached the solver\)
\A(?!(.|\n)*^--path-cov-assert: return: )
\A(?!(.|\n)*^--path-cov-assert: unit '[^']*' -- assumed 2 region bound\(s\) \(0 hole\(s\) punched\) at entry and emitted [0-9]+ candidate assertion\(s\), [1-9])
